<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mu'in al-Din Suleyman Pervane</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1277</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Pervane</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mu'in al-Din Suleyman, known by his title Pervane, was the leading statesman of the Seljuk <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultanate-of-rum">Sultanate of Rum</a> in the 1260s and 1270s, governing under Mongol overlordship. He took the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> port of Sinop in the early 1260s, and his family held it afterwards as a hereditary domain. Suspected of collusion with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baybars">Baybars</a> after the Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elbistan">Elbistan</a>, he was executed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> in 1277.</p></div>
